{
  "scope": "Bounded original Mercs near clipping and world fog execution.\n\nSupply the hash-checked dedicated MERCSW.DLL. Synthetic fixtures execute the\noriginal crossing-edge clip routine 0x1001fee0, with its allocator replaced by\nprivate mapped memory. All arithmetic and interpolation execute unchanged.\nThe polygon near-clip loop 0x100207aa..0x100208ae also executes unchanged;\nits projection callback is intercepted to capture emitted vertices in order.\nThe single-vertex conversion/fog segment 0x100030fa..0x10003248 executes before\nhardware submission, including the original quarter-depth conversion and\nfloat-to-integer helper. There is no graphics driver, full-frame oracle or\noriginal archive I/O in this probe.\n\nOptional --titanium-dll adds execution of the actual Mercs Titanium parser's\npost-scan Z multiplier, camera-height factor and world packet fog calculation.\nTitanium execution stops immediately before its imported MSVCRT _ftol call;\nthe float before that import is original output. The separately named\nstandard_ftol_byte is Python truncation of that float, not a claim to execute\nthe absent Windows CRT. Dedicated _ftol is embedded and executes unchanged.\n\nOptional --world-json accepts a private export from probe_world_assets.c and\nadds the TRA1 TLADUNM polygons identified by the native ID pass. Those vertices\nare read at runtime; no original mesh or executable bytes are embedded here.\nThe camera and near distance in those fixtures are the native capture's,\nnot a claim to have reproduced the complete original camera setup.\n",
  "dll_sha256": "3fe19af50d7f9b7dfab221ee3d4c38e1d1d72454633ef2aee8d6c6c3b0cce383",
  "clip_routine": "0x1001fee0",
  "allocator_stub": "0x10051a00",
  "polygon_clip_segment": "0x100207aa..0x100208ae",
  "projection_capture_stub": "0x1009f26c -> synthetic callback",
  "conversion_fog_segment": "0x100030fa..0x10003248",
  "float_to_int": "0x100733e0",
